./quests/main/0003_conductor/logs/step_0009_implementer.md:537:The health poller will monitor service health by periodically sending HTTP requests to each service's health endpoint. It maintains a map of heartbeat states for each service and uses a timer to schedule polling intervals. The implementation handles various failure cases including network errors, timeouts, invalid responses, and non-2xx status codes. When a service becomes unhealthy, it updates its heartbeat state accordingly and triggers any registered callbacks. The poller can be started and stopped, with proper cleanup of resources when stopped. It uses configurable fetch functions and timing utilities to allow for testing and customization. The poller treats services as unhealthy when they return non-2xx responses, invalid JSON, missing required fields, or fail due to timeouts or network issues. It also considers services unhealthy if they have a healthy:false value in their response. The implementation includes proper error handling and resource cleanup to prevent memory leaks.
