fecycle, and error events are reduced into a focused chat-bubble model for the `sheaf.chatView` webview.\n 7. VS Code document, editor, viewport, and selection changes feed the freshness service, which sends structured context messages when previously observed file, viewport, or cursor state becomes stale.\n \n+## Quest Runner Flow\n+\n+1. The service starts from `projects/quest-runner/start_quest_runner.sh` and binds to port `9002`.\n+2. `POST /create_quest` creates a quest under `projects/<project>/quests/<type>/`, commits the scaffold on the current source branch, and creates the deterministic quest worktree.\n+3. The dashboard lists only project-local quests discovered under `projects/*/quests/`; legacy top-level `quests/` records are hidden.\n+4. Quest detail APIs resolve the matching quest worktree first and use the source checkout only for read-only fallback when the worktree is absent.\n+5. `POST /run_quest` runs the selected quest from its expected worktree and refuses execution when that worktree is missing.\n+6. The v2 runner advances recursive quest and slice machines, invokes role harnesses, enforces path rules from `state_execution_config.yaml`, writes quest-local logs, and commits top-level step metadata to git.\n+\n ## Realtime Agent Components\n \n - `types.ts`: public contracts for events, sessions, tool definitions, callbacks, repositories, and WebSocket injection.\n@@ -57,12 +72,28 @@ The VS Code extension is the editor-facing voice workflow built on top of the re\n - `freshness/*`: change tracking for file reads, viewport observations, cursor observations, and suppression of agent-caused mutation notifications.\n - `statusBar.ts` and `commands.ts`: global VS Code command surface and stateful status bar UX.\n \n+## Quest Runner Components\n+\n+- `api.py`: Flask service endpoints, dashboard shell, and quest lifecycle API surface.\n+- `quest_service.py`: quest creation, run scheduling, locks, and worktree-aware execution boundary.\n+- `quest_fs.py`