uct/PRD.md\n+++ b/docs/product/PRD.md\n@@ -2,13 +2,14 @@\n \n ## Goal\n \n-Sheaf provides a realtime voice workflow for coding. The realtime-agent package supplies a Node/TypeScript library and CLI for live OpenAI Realtime sessions with microphone input, text output, tool calls, and durable event inspection. The VS Code extension embeds that runtime in the editor and exposes VS Code-native read, navigation, and validated write tools for voice-driven coding.\n+Sheaf provides a realtime voice workflow for coding and a project-local quest automation service. The realtime-agent package supplies a Node/TypeScript library and CLI for live OpenAI Realtime sessions with microphone input, text output, tool calls, and durable event inspection. The VS Code extension embeds that runtime in the editor and exposes VS Code-native read, navigation, and validated write tools for voice-driven coding. Quest Runner creates, runs, and monitors repository quests under `projects/<project>/quests/`.\n \n ## Product Surfaces\n \n - Realtime agent CLI: local microphone capture into the OpenAI Realtime API with stdout event visibility and SQLite persistence.\n - Realtime agent library: reusable TypeScript contracts and orchestration primitives for embedding realtime sessions in Node tools.\n - VS Code extension: manual-turn voice coding workflow with Activity Bar chat, global session keybindings, editor context freshness notifications, and the `sheaf VS Code` tool call set.\n+- Quest Runner service: Python REST service and dashboard on port `9002` for project-local quest creation, worktree-based execution, recursive state-machine progress, and run monitoring.\n \n ## Realtime Agent User Flow\n \n@@ -31,6 +32,16 @@ Sheaf provides a realtime voice workflow for coding. The realtime-agent package\n 6. The assistant uses the `sheaf VS Code` tools to read files, inspect visible editor context, move the cursor or viewport, search workspace files, and edit buffers with `modifyFile`.\n 7. The chat pane shows focused user, assistant, tool, context, and error bubbles while suppressing raw protocol noise.\n \n+## Quest Runner User Flow\n+\n+1. User starts the Quest Runner service with `make quest-runner-run`.\n+2. User opens `http://localhost:9002/dashboard`.\n+3. User creates or opens a quest scoped to a Sheaf project under `projects/<project>/quests/`.\n+4. Quest creation writes the quest scaffold on the current source branch and creates a deterministic quest worktree.\n+5. User runs an idle quest from the dashboard or REST API.\n+6. Quest Runner executes from the quest worktree, advances recursive quest and slice state machines, invokes configured role harnesses, writes quest-local logs, and commits step metadata.\n+7. The dashboard shows project identity, quest state, active slice state, issue counts, run status, step history, and git-backed details.\n+\n ## Requirements\n \n - Node 20 or newer.\n@@ -39,6 +50,8 @@ Sheaf provides a realtime voice workflow for coding. The realtime-agent package\n - VS Code 1.85 or newer for the extension.\n - Node/Electron-compatible native dependencies for `better-sqlite3` and `naudiodon`.\n - An open workspace for workspace-scoped VS Code tools.\n+- Python 3 with `projects/quest-runner/requirements.txt` installed in the project virtualenv for Quest Runner.\n+- Git worktree support for Quest Runner quest creation and execution.\n \n ## Current Realtime Agent Capabilities\n \n@@ -67,6 +80,19 @@ Sheaf provides a realtime voice workflow for coding. The realtime-agent package\n - User, formatter, language-server, git, and other non-agent editor changes can trigger structured freshness notifications for previously observed files, cursor state, or viewport state.\n - Agent-caused navigation and `modifyFile` mutations are suppressed from freshness notifications so the model is not warned about its own tool effects.\n \n+## Current Quest Runner Capabilities\n+\n+- Service entry point `quest_runner_service` with `/health`, `/exit`, `/dashboard`, quest lifecycle APIs, and dashboard read APIs.\n+- Project-local quest discovery under `projects/*/quests/`.\n+- Legacy top-level `quests/` exclusion from discovery, dashboard listing, and execution.\n+- Quest creation under `projects/<project>/quests/<type>/` with per-project, per-type numbering.\n+- Immediate deterministic worktree creation using `<project>_<quest_type>_<number>_<slug>` and branch `quest/<worktree_name>`.\n+- Worktree-based `run_quest` execution with explicit refusal when the expected worktree is missing.\n+- Recursive v2 quest and slice state machines, normalized quest-root state files, legacy slice state files, and git step metadata.\n+- Role harness invocation through quest-local `state_execution_config.yaml` profiles and path-rule enforcement.\n+- Web dashboard for projects, quest overview, slice pages, issue summaries, agent logs, run status, and git commits/diffs.\n+- Runtime service logs under `logs/quest-runner/` and quest step logs inside each quest directory.\n+\n ## Non-Goals\n \n - Audio output playback.\n@@ -75,6 +101,8 @@ Sheaf provides a realtime voice workflow for coding. The realtime-agent package\n - Protocol-level session resume after connection loss.\n - Retention or deletion policy for persisted realtime records.\n - Direct shell, filesystem, or external patch writes from the VS Code tool set; editor writes go through VS Code buffer APIs.\n+- Quest Runner migration of legacy top-level quest records.\n+- Quest Runner service orchestration, SQLite/database state, service log streaming, or MCP endpoints.\n \n ## Success Criteria\n \n@@ -83,3 +111,4 @@ Sheaf provides a realtime voice workflow for coding. The realtime-agent package\n - Tool calls are observable, serial, and error-tolerant.\n - Operators can inspect non-audio realtime behavior through stdout and SQLite.\n - VS Code users can run a manual-turn voice session, inspect conversation/tool activity in the chat pane, and edit workspace buffers through validated `mo