osts, deterministic session-controller tests, tool contract tests, and freshness service tests.\n \n+## Quest Runner: Current Capabilities\n+\n+- Project entry point: `projects/quest-runner`, registered in the root Makefile and `config/services.json`.\n+- Service surface: `/health`, `/exit`, `/dashboard`, `/create_quest`, `/run_quest`, and `/api/dashboard/*`.\n+- Storage model: project-local quests under `projects/<project>/quests/`; legacy top-level `quests/` records are ignored.\n+- Creation model: quest scaffold commit on the current source branch followed by deterministic worktree creation.\n+- Execution model: `run_quest` executes inside the expected quest worktree and reports missing worktrees as operational errors.\n+- Runner model: recursive v2 quest and slice state machines, role harnesses, path-rule enforcement, human-intervention blocks, and git step metadata.\n+- Dashboard model: project selector, quest overview, run control, slice pages, issue views, agent logs, run overlays, and git-backed commit/diff views.\n+- Operations model: service logs under `logs/quest-runner/`; quest step logs inside each quest directory; no SQLite or persistent service database.\n+\n ## Realtime Agent: Next Product Work\n \n - Add a named tool-call-set registry so operators can choose reusable tool bundles by stable names.\n@@ -55,11 +69,20 @@ The VS Code extension foundation embeds the realtime-agent library in the extens\n - Continue hardening tool summaries and context bubbles so the chat pane stays useful without exposing raw protocol events.\n - Evaluate additional editor tools only when they preserve the VS Code-buffer-first contract.\n \n+## Quest Runner: Next Product Work\n+\n+- Add a later migration path for selected legacy top-level quest records into project-local layout.\n+- Continue improving dashboard operator affordances around paused runs, missing worktrees, and human-intervention requests.\n+- Expand service-level smoke guidance for running Quest Runner together with Conductor-managed service registration.\n+- Keep quest schema docs synchronized between bundled runtime prompt references and human-facing project docs.\n+\n ## Engineering Constraints\n \n - Keep behavior documented in present tense and tied to code in the repository.\n - Preserve clear boundaries between the realtime-agent library and the VS Code extension host integration.\n - Preserve clear boundaries between VS Code buffer tools and direct filesystem/shell mutation paths.\n+- Preserve clear boundaries between Quest Runner and the Conductor service orchestrator.\n+- Keep Quest Runner quest state filesystem-backed and project-local; do not introduce a persistent quest database.\n - Prefer focused vertical changes with corresponding tests.\n - Do not persist or print raw outgoing realtime audio append payloads.\n - Treat unexpected realtime socket close as terminal for the current session.\ndiff --git a/docs/testing/TEST_STRATEGY.md b/docs/testing/TEST_STRATEGY.md\nindex ef61b17..b840360 100644\n--- a/docs/testing/TEST_STRATEGY.md\n+++ b/docs/testing/TEST_STRATEGY.md\n@@ -4,7 +4,9 @@\n \n - Preserve realtime-agent public TypeScript contracts and session orchestration behavior.\n - Preserve VS Code extension session controls, read/navigation/write tool contracts, chat reduction behavior, and context freshness notifications.\n+- Preserve Quest Runner project-local quest creation, discovery, worktree execution boundaries, recursive state-machine behavior, and dashboard APIs.\n - Validate realtime persistence, event routing, tool dispatch, response queueing, and transport error handling.\n+- Validate that Quest Runner excludes legacy top-level quests and does not reintroduce service-orchestrator, SQLite, database, log-streaming, or MCP behavior.\n - Keep live-device behavior covered by manual smoke checks where automation cannot reliably exercise local permissions or hardware.\n \n ## Automated Test Layers\n@@ -14,6 +16,7 @@\n - Realtime transport tests: WebSocket URL/header construction, JSON send/receive, invalid message handling, close handling, and fake socket integration.\n - Realtime CLI tests: argument parsing, required prompt/context files, required `OPENAI_API_KEY`, unknown tool handling, signal-style shutdown, and dependency-injected runtime startup.\n - VS Code extension TypeScript unit tests: session controller lifecycle, command wiring, chat model summaries, tool dispatcher wiring, read/navigation tool contracts, `modifyFile` validation/edit contracts, and freshness service behavior.\n+- Quest Runner Python unit tests: service endpoints, project-local quest model, quest creation, deterministic worktrees, worktree execution paths, dashboard payloads, dashboard assets, normalized quest state, recursive state machines, commit metadata, harness/thread helpers, and migration-boundary validation.\n \n ## Commands\n \n@@ -22,6 +25,7 @@ From the repository root:\n ```bash\n make test-realtime-agent\n make test-vscode-extension\n+make quest-runner-test\n ```\n \n From the realtime-agent package:\n@@ -46,11 +50,24 @@ The extension test command compiles tests into `.test-dist` and runs them with N\n \n `modifyFile` coverage verifies the registered `sheaf VS Code` tool set name, stable legacy read/navigation tool names, single-line and multi-line replacements, zero-length insertion, exact target/context mismatch failures, compact mismatch details, no partial edit on failure, file/position validation, and suppression of self-generated freshness notifications.\n \n+From the Quest Runner project:\n+\n+```bash\n+cd projects/quest-runner\n+make test\n+```\n+\n+The Quest Runner test target creates a project virtualenv from\n+`requirements.txt`, sets `PYTHONPATH=src`, and runs the curated `unittest` module\n+list in `projects/quest-runner/Makefile`.\n+\n ## Minimum Checks Before Merging\n \n - `npm test` in `apps/realtime-agent` for realtime-agent changes.\n - `npm test` in `apps/vscode-extension` for VS Code extension changes.\n+- `make quest-runner-test` for Quest Runner service, dashboard, quest filesystem, worktree, or state-machine changes.\n - Both package tests for shared documentation or repository-level workflow changes.\n+- Include Quest Runner tests for repository-level workflow changes that affect `projects/`, Makefile forwarding, service registration, quest docs, or quest directory behavior.\n \n ## Manual Checks\n \n@@ -68,3 +85,12 @@ The extension test command compiles tests into `.test-dist` and runs them with N\n   - verify a simple `modifyFile` edit changes the active VS Code buffer through the editor and remains undoable in VS Code\n   - edit an observed file manually and verify the agent receives a freshness context bubble before it writes again\n   - press `F16` again to stop and confirm return to idle\n+- Quest Runner service smoke run:\n+  - run `make quest-runner-run`\n+  - verify `curl -s http://localhost:9002/health`\n+  - open `http://localhost:9002/dashboard`\n+  - confirm only `projects/*/quests/` records are listed\n+  - create a project-local quest through `POST /create_quest` or the dashboard flow\n+  - confirm the deterministic `.quest-worktrees/<project>_<type>_<number>_<slug>` worktree exists\n+  - run an idle quest through the dashboard run control or `POST /run_quest`\n+  - confirm service logs appear under `logs/quest-runner/` and step logs appear inside the quest directory\n", "command": "/bin/bash -lc 'git diff -- docs'", "exit_code": 0, "id": "item_41", "status": "completed", "type": "command_execution"}, "type": "item.completed"}, "provider_thread_id": "019ea035-b25d-7f61-a43b-e90d31840651", "role": "documenter", "schema_version": 1, "sequence": 80, "step": 23, "thread": "Sheaf_quest_0004_documenter", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T03:56:37Z"}
./quests/main/0004_migratequest_runner/logs/step_0023_documenter.jsonl:95:{"event_kind": "provider.json", "harness": "codex", "payload": {"item": {"aggregated_output": "# Quest Runner Operations\n\n## Purpose\n\nQuest Runner is a Sheaf project service in `projects/quest-runner`. It creates,\nruns, and monitors filesystem-backed quests under `projects/<project>/quests/`.\nIt runs on port `9002`, serves a web dashboard at `/dashboard`, exposes REST\nAPIs for quest creation and execution, and executes quest role harnesses through\nthe recursive quest state machine.\n\nQuest Runner is separate from the Conductor service orchestrator. It does not\nmanage other services, expose MCP routes, stream service logs, use SQLite, or\nmaintain a database-backed quest index.\n\n## Build And Run\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```bash\nmake quest-runner-test\nmake quest-runner-run\n```\n\nFrom the project directory:\n\n```bash\nmake -C projects/quest-runner test\nmake -C projects/quest-runner run\n```\n\nThe run target invokes `projects/quest-runner/start_quest_runner.sh`, which\ncreates the project virtualenv when needed, sets `PYTHONPATH` to\n`projects/quest-runner/src`, and starts:\n\n```bash\npython -m quest_runner_service --port 9002\n```\n\n## Service Endpoints\n\n- `GET /health`: returns `{ \"healthy\": true, \"uptime\": <seconds> }`.\n- `POST /exit`: exits the service cleanly for service-manager integration.\n- `GET /dashboard`: serves the Quest Runner dashboard shell.\n- `POST /create_quest`: creates a project-local quest and immediately creates\n  the deterministic quest worktree.\n- `POST /run_quest`: schedules execution for an existing project-local quest.\n\nDashboard read APIs live under `/api/dashboard/*`. Quest-addressing endpoints\nuse project identity, quest type, and quest number so links and actions stay\nscoped to `projects/<project>/quests/`.\n\nFull project-local API reference:\n`projects/quest-runner/docs/reference/api.md`.\n\n## Quest Storage\n\nQuest Runner treats this layout as canonical:\n\n```text\nprojects/<project>/quests/\n  main|side/\n    0000_example_slug/\n      meta.json\n      state.md\n      state_history.md\n      thread_registry.json\n      physicalplan_issues.md\n      state_execution_config.yaml\n      specs/\n      slices/\n      logs/\n      threads/\n```\n\nQuest numbering is scoped by project and quest type. The same numeric quest id\ncan exist in different projects. Quest metadata includes project identity in\n`meta.json`; readers can also derive the project from the path when older records\ndo not include that field.\n\nThe legacy top-level `quests/` tree remains on disk for historical records but\nis not scanned by the Quest Runner service, dashboard, or runner.\n\n## Worktrees\n\nQuest creation happens on the current source checkout branch and immediately\ncreates a matching git worktree. The deterministic worktree name is:\n\n```text\n<project>_<quest_type>_<number>_<slug>\n```\n\nWorktrees live at:\n\n```text\n<repo-parent>/.quest-worktrees/<worktree_name>/\n```\n\nThe worktree branch is `quest/<worktree_name>`. `run_quest` executes inside the\nexpected quest worktree and returns an operational error when that worktree is\nmissing; it does not silently recreate worktrees for existing quests.\n\n## Dashboard Behavior\n\nThe dashboard lists only projects that contain project-local quests. Quest detail\nURLs and API calls include project identity. For existing quests, dashboard reads\nprefer the matching quest worktree when it exists and fall back to the source\ncheckout for read-only discovery and creation flows when no worktree is present.\n\nThe overview page shows quest state, active slice state, issue counts, run\nstatus, step history, and git-backed metadata. When a quest is idle and runnable,\nthe overview includes a run control that calls `POST /run_quest`.\n\nThe dashboard intentionally has no service-management pages, service restart\ncontrols, service log streaming UI, database view, or MCP configuration.\n\n## Runner Lifecycle\n\nThe runner preserves the v2 recursive state-machine model:\n\n- quest-root `state.md` is normalized after v2 runner commits;\n- slice `state.md` files keep the legacy slice state schema;\n- role harness turns are recorded in the quest directory;\n- each successful top-level runner step creates a git commit with recursive\n  state-machine metadata;\n- no-op top-level steps skip commits and do not increment `global_step`;\n- human-intervention files block automatic progress until resolved.\n\nQuest-local `state_execution_config.yaml` controls role harness profiles and\npath-rule enforcement. The service refuses to invoke harnesses when the target\nrepository working tree is not clean.\n\n## Logs And Runtime Data\n\nService logs are written under:\n\n```text\nlogs/quest-runner/\n  quest-runner.log\n  quest_runner_stdout.log\n  quest_runner_stderr.log\n```\n\nQuest execution artifacts stay with the active quest, including files such as:\n\n```text\nprojects/<project>/quests/<type>/<number>_<slug>/logs/step_<n>_<role>.jsonl\n```\n\nQuest Runner does not use SQLite or another persistent database for quest state,\nservice state, dashboard state, or discovery.\n\n## Configuration\n\nThe service is registered in `config/services.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"quest-runner\",\n  \"host\": \"0.0.0.0\",\n  \"port\": 9002,\n  \"home_path\": \"/dashboard\",\n  \"command\": \"make quest-runner-run\"\n}\n```\n\nPersistent quest behavior is configured per quest through\n`state_execution_config.yaml`. The project also ships a default config at\n`projects/quest-runner/src/quest_runner_service/default_state_execution_config.yaml`.\n\n## Testing\n\nQuest Runner tests run with:\n\n```bash\nmake quest-runner-test\n```\n\nCoverage includes project-local quest creation and discovery, deterministic\nworktree naming, dashboard project identity, legacy top-level quest exclusion,\nworktree-based execution, missing-worktree refusal, recursive state metadata,\ndashboard assets, service endpoints, and migration-boundary checks that exclude\nSQLite, MCP, and service-orchestrator behavior.\n\nProject-local docs are indexed at `projects/quest-runner/docs/README.md`.\n", "command": "/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/operations/QUEST_RUNNER.md\"", "exit_code": 0, "id": "item_49", "status": "completed", "type": "command_execution"}, "type": "item.completed"}, "provider_thread_id": "019ea035-b25d-7f61-a43b-e90d31840651", "role": "documenter", "schema_version": 1, "sequence": 95, "step": 23, "thread": "Sheaf_quest_0004_documenter", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T03:56:59Z"}
