./projects/sheaf-chat/quests/main/0000_sheaf_chat/logs/step_0031_polisher_reviewer.jsonl:959:{"event_kind": "provider.json", "harness": "claude_code", "payload": {"message": {"content": [{"text": "Temp files cleaned up; the only changes are the CLI-managed issue files. My review is complete.\n\n## Review summary — slice 0005 `pi_agent_lifecycle`\n\nI reviewed the implemented slice against the physical plan and slice spec: `lifecycle.ts`, `summarizer.ts`, `piAdapter.ts`, `sessionRuntime.ts`, `manager.ts`, and the lifecycle tests. Overall the implementation matches the plan well — state transitions, manifest deferral, summary fallback, hot/cold resume, steer/followUp, model switching, cancellation, and idle-offload guards are all present and covered by tests.\n\nI filed **two open polishing issues**:\n\n- **PL-0001 (primary, medium-high):** `LifecycleEmitter.EmitError` emits on Node's **reserved `\"error\"` event**. With no `\"error\"` listener registered (none is, by default), `emit(\"error\", obj)` throws `ERR_UNHANDLED_ERROR`. This defeats the intended *non-fatal* delivery-error reporting in `AcceptUserMessage`, risks an **unhandled-promise-rejection crash** on the fire-and-forget manifest-write path (`HandleAssistantMessageCompleted`), and can mask the typed `AgentManagerError` on the startup-failure path. Untested — no test exercises an error emit with zero subscribers.\n- **PL-0002 (low):** `SessionRuntimeRecord.lastError` is declared and surfaced via `AgentStatusSnapshot.error`, but never assigned — so `getStatus().error` is always `undefined`, leaving pull-based status consumers blind to failure reasons (dead field / incomplete API).\n\nThings I checked and deliberately did **not** flag:\n- The plan suggests `SessionManager.create` for new sessions, but the adapter always uses `SessionManager.open(filePath, …)`. This is the *correct* choice here — `create` generates its own timestamped filename, which would break Sheaf's deterministic `${sessionId}.jsonl` naming; `open` on the empty shell file is handled by Pi (`setSessionFile` → `newSession` → rewrite). The unused `coldResume` param is a minor smell only, not a defect.\n\nSince open issues remain, I did not create `implementation_accepted.md`. The polisher should address PL-0001 (and PL-0002) before acceptance.", "type": "text"}], "context_management": null, "diagnostics": null, "id": "msg_01Sn2Y5mYHo44sL1k8XFeMFv", "model": "claude-opus-4-8", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 292, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 292, "cache_read_input_tokens": 91286, "inference_geo": "not_available", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard"}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "request_id": "req_011CbrZnc5nmJQH6FnADgusD", "session_id": "908a34fb-6e31-45a3-af16-dae436832fe2", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "626cf7ec-81c5-4fd5-8a61-0248c90b3c70"}, "provider_thread_id": "908a34fb-6e31-45a3-af16-dae436832fe2", "role": "polisher_reviewer", "schema_version": 1, "sequence": 959, "step": 31, "thread": "sheaf-chat_main_0000_sheaf_chat_quest_0000_slice_0005_polisher_reviewer", "timestamp": "2026-06-08T22:16:49Z"}
./projects/sheaf-chat/quests/main/0000_sheaf_chat/logs/step_0031_polisher_reviewer.jsonl:963:{"event_kind": "provider.json", "harness": "claude_code", "payload": {"api_error_status": null, "duration_api_ms": 325436, "duration_ms": 327024, "fast_mode_state": "off", "is_error": false, "modelUsage": {"claude-opus-4-8": {"cacheCreationInputTokens": 75762, "cacheReadInputTokens": 1902389, "contextWindow": 1000000, "costUSD": 1.961687, "inputTokens": 806, "maxOutputTokens": 64000, "outputTokens": 21318, "webSearchRequests": 0}}, "num_turns": 44, "permission_denials": [{"tool_input": {"command": "cd projects/sheaf-chat && grep -rn \"SessionManager\" src/ node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist/*.d.ts 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"create\\|open\\|static\" | head -30", "description": "Inspect SessionManager API"}, "tool_name": "Bash", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01TYsdDQJLbdNDE9t1bHo2rY"}, {"tool_input": {"command": "node -e '\nconst { EventEmitter } = require(\"node:events\");\nconst e = new EventEmitter();\ntry {\n  e.emit(\"error\", { key: \"k\", code: \"c\", message: \"m\" });\n  console.log(\"emit returned normally (no throw)\");\n} catch (err) {\n  console.log(\"THREW:\", err && err.code, \"-\", err && err.message);\n}\n'", "description": "Verify emit error with no listener throws"}, "tool_name": "Bash", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Vvqbi8iSG8u21m7eUuhr2w"}, {"tool_input": {"command": "/Users/joyo/.quest-worktrees/sheaf-chat_main_0000_sheaf_chat/scripts/quest-runner issues create --help 2>&1 | head -40", "description": "Show issues create help via absolute path"}, "tool_name": "Bash", "tool_use_id": "toolu_018ctp933Aqj7kNnwzQRsR1v"}, {"tool_input": {"command": "/Users/joyo/.quest-worktrees/sheaf-chat_main_0000_sheaf_chat/scripts/quest-runner issues create --help", "description": "Show issues create help"}, "tool_name": "Bash", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01B31cUmKHJa6zyZ5ZjywgPU"}, {"tool_input": {"command": "cat > /tmp/issue_error_event.md <<'EOF'\n## Problem\n\n`LifecycleEmitter` (src/agents/lifecycle.ts) extends Node's `EventEmitter` and emits\nlifecycle errors on the **reserved `\"error\"` event name**:\n\n```ts\nEmitError(event: LifecycleErrorEvent): void {\n  this.emit(\"error\", event);\n}\n```\n\nNode's `EventEmitter` gives `\"error\"` special semantics: if `emit(\"error\", …)` is\ncalled and **no listener is registered for `\"error\"`**, Node throws. Because the\npayload here is a plain object (not an `Error`), it throws an `ERR_UNHANDLED_ERROR`\n(`Unhandled 'error' event`). Nothing in this slice registers a default `\"error\"`\nlistener on the emitter (verified: `grep` of src/ finds only the `emit(\"error\", …)`\ncall and the type union member; `LifecycleEmitter` has no constructor / no default\nlistener). The emitter is created in `AgentManager.Create` with no internal\nsubscriber, and slice 8 (the WebSocket bridge) is what is expected to attach\nlisteners later.\n\n## Why this is a problem\n\nThe error-reporting paths are reachable on ordinary (non-test) flows, and the throw\ndefeats their intent:\n\n1. **Non-fatal delivery errors become thrown rejections.**\n   `SessionRuntime.AcceptUserMessage` catches a Pi delivery failure and calls\n   `EmitError({ code: \"user_message_delivery_failed\", fatal: false })` specifically so\n   the message is *reported* rather than thrown (the plan requires \"the manager must\n   report acceptance before Pi failure can drop it\"). With no `\"error\"` listener, the\n   `emit` itself throws, so `AcceptUserMessage` rejects and `submitUserMessage`\n   rejects — the opposite of the intended non-fatal reporting.\n\n2. **Process-level crash risk on the manifest-write path.**\n   `HandlePiEvent` triggers `void this.HandleAssistantMessageCompleted()`\n   (fire-and-forget). If the initial manifest write fails (disk/permission/etc.), its\n   catch calls `EmitError({ code: \"manifest_write_failed\" })`. With no listener, the\n   throw surfaces inside an unawaited promise → **unhandled promise rejection**, which\n   can terminate the process. This is triggered by a normal event (assistant message\n   completion), not just an exotic error path.\n\n3. **Startup-failure path throws the wrong error.**\n   `AgentManager.StartSessionRuntime`'s catch calls `EmitError({ fatal: true })` and\n   *then* `throw new AgentManagerError(\"session_start_failed\", …)`. If `EmitError`\n   throws first, callers receive an `ERR_UNHANDLED_ERROR` instead of the intended\n   typed `AgentManagerError`.\n\nThis is the classic `EventEmitter` `\"error\"` footgun. It is currently masked only\nbecause no test exercises an `EmitError` path without first attaching a listener.\n\n## Test coverage gap\n\nNo test drives any `EmitError` path with zero `\"error\"` subscribers (the existing\nsummarizer-failure test uses the deterministic fallback and emits no error). A\nregression test that calls a manager/runtime error path on an emitter with no\n`\"error\"` listener would have caught this.\n\n## What must be true to close\n\n- Emitting a lifecycle error when no consumer is subscribed must not throw or cause an\n  unhandled rejection. Acceptable resolutions include: renaming the lifecycle error\n  event off the reserved `\"error\"` name, registering a safe default no-op `\"error\"`\n  listener in the `LifecycleEmitter` constructor, or otherwise guarding the emit so a\n  missing listener is a no-op.\n- The non-fatal delivery-error path (`AcceptUserMessage`) and the fire-and-forget\n  manifest-write path (`HandleAssistantMessageCompleted`) must not reject/crash when\n  no `\"error\"` listener is attached.\n- A test covers emitting a lifecycle error with no subscriber and asserts no throw /\n  no unhandled rejection.\nEOF\nscripts/quest-runner issues create --project sheaf-chat --type main --number 0 --scope polishing --slice 5 --title \"LifecycleEmitter emits on reserved \\\"error\\\" event; throws/crashes when no listener is attached\" --body-file /tmp/issue_error_event.md", "description": "Create primary issue for error-event footgun"}, "tool_name": "Bash", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01C257mVoSygvoW1rX7ZD6Ky"}], "result": "Temp files cleaned up; the only changes are the CLI-managed issue files. My review is complete.\n\n## Review summary — slice 0005 `pi_agent_lifecycle`\n\nI reviewed the implemented slice against the physical plan and slice spec: `lifecycle.ts`, `summarizer.ts`, `piAdapter.ts`, `sessionRuntime.ts`, `manager.ts`, and the lifecycle tests. Overall the implementation matches the plan well — state transitions, manifest deferral, summary fallback, hot/cold resume, steer/followUp, model switching, cancellation, and idle-offload guards are all present and covered by tests.\n\nI filed **two open polishing issues**:\n\n- **PL-0001 (primary, medium-high):** `LifecycleEmitter.EmitError` emits on Node's **reserved `\"error\"` event**. With no `\"error\"` listener registered (none is, by default), `emit(\"error\", obj)` throws `ERR_UNHANDLED_ERROR`. This defeats the intended *non-fatal* delivery-error reporting in `AcceptUserMessage`, risks an **unhandled-promise-rejection crash** on the fire-and-forget manifest-write path (`HandleAssistantMessageCompleted`), and can mask the typed `AgentManagerError` on the startup-failure path. Untested — no test exercises an error emit with zero subscribers.\n- **PL-0002 (low):** `SessionRuntimeRecord.lastError` is declared and surfaced via `AgentStatusSnapshot.error`, but never assigned — so `getStatus().error` is always `undefined`, leaving pull-based status consumers blind to failure reasons (dead field / incomplete API).\n\nThings I checked and deliberately did **not** flag:\n- The plan suggests `SessionManager.create` for new sessions, but the adapter always uses `SessionManager.open(filePath, …)`. This is the *correct* choice here — `create` generates its own timestamped filename, which would break Sheaf's deterministic `${sessionId}.jsonl` naming; `open` on the empty shell file is handled by Pi (`setSessionFile` → `newSession` → rewrite). The unused `coldResume` param is a minor smell only, not a defect.\n\nSince open issues remain, I did not create `implementation_accepted.md`. The polisher should address PL-0001 (and PL-0002) before acceptance.", "session_id": "908a34fb-6e31-45a3-af16-dae436832fe2", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "subtype": "success", "terminal_reason": "completed", "time_to_request_ms": 45, "total_cost_usd": 1.961687, "ttft_ms": 3434, "ttft_stream_ms": 2901, "type": "result", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 75762, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 75762, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1902389, "inference_geo": "not_available", "input_tokens": 806, "iterations": [{"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 292, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 292, "cache_read_input_tokens": 91286, "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 809, "type": "message"}], "output_tokens": 21318, "server_tool_use": {"web_fetch_requests": 0, "web_search_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "uuid": "db6e2be8-5f1d-4e2e-aee3-e05be1955470"}, "provider_thread_id": "908a34fb-6e31-45a3-af16-dae436832fe2", "role": "polisher_reviewer", "schema_version": 1, "sequence": 963, "step": 31, "thread": "sheaf-chat_main_0000_sheaf_chat_quest_0000_slice_0005_polisher_reviewer", "timestamp": "2026-06-08T22:16:49Z"}
